  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'Everything is real-time: nothing is baked. Every light, reflection and fog effect updates as soon as a value changes.'
--- !u!114 &-4447444718013889139
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'A night gas station in fog and rain: a canopy with six fluorescent fixtures over two fuel pumps, a small kiosk with warm windows, a wet concrete forecourt, haze and light shafts. This tutorial builds it in the order the layers of a look depend on each other: first the objects and their materials, then the camera, the night sky, the lights, the reflections, the fog, the rain and the post-processing. Every layer is saved before the next one starts, so each step can be compared with the one before.'
