--- !u!114 &-2213911973277336602
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "<b>The Hierarchy by layer.</b> In the finished scene, the Hierarchy has one parent per layer, numbered like the sections of this tutorial: <i>1-4 \xB7 Objects</i>, <i>6 \xB7 Wet Ground</i>, <i>7 \xB7 Camera</i>, <i>9 \xB7 Lights</i>, <i>10 \xB7 Fog</i>, <i>11 \xB7 Reflections</i>, <i>12 \xB7 Rain</i>, and <i>10-13 \xB7 Volume (fog, reflections, post)</i>. Switch a parent off (the checkbox at the top of the Inspector) to see what its layer adds to the frame. Build your own scene with the same parents."
